2. `recordExecutionBlocked` in completeTask/cancelTask is called with 4 args (incidentId, taskId, actor, "COMPLETE") but the method signature has 5 (with now). Let me check what I wrote in completeTask: `recordExecutionBlocked(incident.id(), task.id(), actor, "COMPLETE");` — 4 args. Need to fix those calls to pass now(). In completeTask, `now` variable — I compute `Set<Long> expiredNow = materializeExpirations(incident.id(), actor, now());` then later `Instant now = now();` declared after the blocker check. The interception branch occurs before `now` is declared. Let me fix: in completeTask/cancelTask, declare `Instant now = now();` at the top and reuse. Let me review the completeTask code I wrote:

```java
requireCommander(incident, actor);
Set<Long> expiredNow = materializeExpirations(incident.id(), actor, now());
IncidentTask task = ...;
if (expiredNow.contains(task.id())) {
    recordExecutionBlocked(incident.id(), task.id(), actor, "COMPLETE");
    return ...;
}
...
Instant now = now();
tasks.markDone(task.id(), actor, now);
